 "note": "RealBox (customer enclosure) hand-built collision boxes, metres. Frames: origin at the lowest point of each part (tray: base centre; circuit: lowest visual point; cap: tab bottoms), xy at the part bbox centre. Tray/cap boxes measured from the STEP meshes by ray-grid scans (0.25-0.5 mm). Circuit boxes inherited from the orel-repo circuit_boxes.json (plate 3-way split leaves 0.3 mm corner pockets for the cap tabs; assumes board corner notches, customer question pending). Cap tabs shaved 0.1 mm/side in x (insertion draft approximation; exact would be a zero-clearance fit). Cap seat: tabs rest on the tray corner posts (post top 11.1 mm, tab bottom at seat ~11.3 mm on the SDF model; boxes seat 0.2 mm lower on the posts).",
 "circuit_note": "clipped to board footprint -1.5mm; under-wall boxes flattened to 0.2mm; y-edge terminal boxes z<=12.4mm board frame (cap louver slat undersides sit at 12.8; terminals pass through the louver windows in the real part) | 2026-07-24 run16: plate box re-clipped to cavity-fit 121.4x87.4mm on TRUE plate centre (plate 123x88 rectangle; bbox y=89.5 includes overhanging parts -> plate centre y=-0.75 in bbox frame); real plate exceeds the 122x88 cavity by 0.5mm/side in x and matches y exactly (CAD interference, question to customer) - box models an effective 0.3mm/side running fit so the cavity walls provide the lateral constraint. Y-edge terminal boxes clamped to z<=0.0024 centred (0.5mm below the cap louver slats at the fully seated pose, slats measured at 25.20 world by 0.25mm ray grid); prior 12.4 board-frame clamp left only 0.11mm - inside SDF-error + tilt noise, so the cap weight leaked through the circuit instead of the tray rim. | 2026-07-25 cap rev2 (corner-tab skirt): plate box split into 3 (centre slab + two x-end strips) leaving the 4 corner pockets open with 0.3mm margin for the cap tabs (10.25x8.75mm, bottoms 11.2mm world at seat) - ASSUMES the real board has corner notches, since the CAD tabs pass 1.49mm through the plate corners at the seated pose (customer question #7). Lateral wall constraint preserved via the end strips (x +-60.7) and slab y edges.",
